<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Economou et al. (2012) FGF10/FGF7-SHH activator-inhibitor Turing stripe mechanism at mammalian palatal growth zones — Code-to-model traceability: 68/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Functions compute J_0, Re(sigma(q)), and 1D reaction-diffusion dynamics (L36-145), but lack explicit equation-level docstrings cross-referencing Economou et al. (2012) Figs. 1-4, Pantalacci et al. (2008), Welsh & O'Brien (2009), and the 3 Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_008_palate_ruguga_turing.lean`." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py L36–L145: Brief docstrings without explicit paper figure/equation or Lean 4 theorem mappings <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45d4150/2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py#L36-L145>" ;
    pk:hasScore 6.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Economou et al. (2012) FGF10/FGF7-SHH activator-inhibitor Turing stripe mechanism at mammalian palatal growth zones — Model fidelity to source: 58/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Implements the 2x2 FGF-SHH activator-inhibitor Jacobian J_0 (L36-43), dispersion curve Re(sigma(q)) (L46-85), and 1D reaction-diffusion solver (L88-145), backed by 3 Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_008_palate_ruguga_turing.lean`. However, it integrates only a static fixed-length 1D domain without modeling 2D anteroposterior growth-zone elongation anterior to ruga 8 (`8 -> 1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4 -> 5 -> 6 -> 7 -> 7b`) or the equal-diffusion (D_A = D_H) negative control." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py L88–L145: Static 1D fixed-length solver without 2D ruga-8 growth-zone sequential intercalation or equal-diffusion negative control <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45d4150/2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py#L88-L145>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-model-fidelity-1> ;
    pk:hasScore 5.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Economou et al. (2012) FGF10/FGF7-SHH activator-inhibitor Turing stripe mechanism at mammalian palatal growth zones — Morphometric validation: 55/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L234-267) returns only 3 baseline metrics (lambda_c, r(FGF, SHH), and 1D wild-type rugae count) without evaluating the 9-stage sequential growth-zone intercalation regression (Pearson r, p-value, RMSE), coronal vs sagittal cut stripe anisotropy / bifurcation index, cyclopamine / FGF10 perturbation counts, or computer-vision segmentation of left and right palatal shelf rugae in the biological specimen." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
